r inspection is summarized below. If $X$ is the number of defective components found in an inspection, what is the expected value of $X?$\n\n| Number of Inspections | $5$ | $7$ | $4$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Defects | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536072 true] [17592186382280 1113 #uuid "d560fb15-db9a-5490-82a8-59b971388ae3" 13194139536072 true] [17592186382280 1145 "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the defects, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of inspections is $5+7+4+3+1=20,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{5}{20} \\\\ P(X=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{7}{20} \\\\ P(X=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{4}{20} \\\\ P(X=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{3}{20} \\\\ P(X=4)=f(4) & =\\frac{1}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{5}{20}$ | $\\frac{7}{20}$ | $\\frac{4}{20}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{5}{20})+1(\\frac{7}{20})+2(\\frac{4}{20})+3(\\frac{3}{20})+4(\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}+\\frac{8}{20}+\\frac{9}{20}+\\frac{4}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536072 true] [17592186382281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382282 13194139536072 true] [17592186382281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382283 13194139536072 true] [17592186382281 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536072 true] [17592186382281 1041 "field-1" 13194139536072 true] [17592186382281 1104 #edb/ref 175921